# LF everywhere. INV-5a's byte-identical round trip does not survive CRLF, and an
# editor with a misconfigured core.autocrlf, or an edit made through the GitHub web
# UI, would otherwise break `jamground-validate --check` on their first save.
#
# This file is a convenience, not the gate. The gate is jamground-validate reading raw
# bytes and rejecting any \r, any BOM, any trailing whitespace, any tab, and any file
# not ending in exactly one \n (site repo, docs/02 §10).
* text=auto eol=lf

*.yaml   text eol=lf
*.yml    text eol=lf
*.md     text eol=lf
*.svg    text eol=lf

content/media/*.jpg  binary
content/media/*.png  binary
content/media/*.webp binary
content/media/*.avif binary
content/media/*.gif  binary
